{
  "key": "estuary",
  "name": "Estuary",
  "name_bn": "\u09ae\u09cb\u09b9\u09a8\u09be",
  "premise": "Quiet editorial competence. A deep green-teal ground against a bone paper, with the warmth coming from the paper rather than from a second expressive colour. Barishal sits in a river delta; an estuary is where fresh water meets salt, which is also what a studio serving two audiences in two scripts is doing. This is Direction A: the existing draft, corrected. One correction is substantive \u2014 the draft declares no accent at all, and a system whose accent equals its text colour cannot express a link, a selected row, or a primary action. A cyan-teal accent is therefore introduced: a near neighbour of the ground, discriminable from it, and still honouring 'no second expressive colour'.",
  "generated_by": "05_colour/engine.py",
